Orca: the finish-fix stage fixed 8 of 9 lens-0 whole-diff findings at 9caac0a9cd (pushed to yasyf/orca cc-sync/cross-machine-recovery), with tests that fail first:
- resume keeps the dormant record as its fence until ensureAgentSession succeeds, and holds are exclusive;
- requireFreshPane refuses an adopted placement → recovery_placement_occupied;
- provenance updates are serialized;
- a failed "Start shell instead" restores the record;
- per-pane binding reservation;
- per-worktree import serialization (concurrent first imports);
- the frame budget counts untrimmed bytes;
- merge-records returns the actually-held records;
- persisted launchPreferences for deferred Resume.
Finding 6 reproduction 2 (a binding-less import crash before provenance can never be retried) remained. Per the root fix-group guidance, the coordinator stopped that serial workflow before QA and deleted an untracked reviewer scratch test file it left behind (never committed). The replacement is Run wf_96a9397c-ea4:
- triage of the remaining item + the 8 reproduced lens-1-rerun findings (reviews/orca-lens1-rerun.md), with already-fixed overlaps listed with evidence, into 2–4 parallel groups with single-owner files;
- failing-first fixes in isolated worktrees (branches cc-sync/xmr-fix-<group> from 9caac0a);
- a merge, then TARGETED per-group astra refutation (no new whole review);
- ONE hidden rendered QA pass (ORCA_BACKGROUND_LAUNCH=1): the picker spec (env scrub, divergence re-run targeting, cancel, newer_partial, not_restorable, local header with a remote env active) and a two-profile import/export e2e (recoveryLaunch argv, no-PTY placeholders incl. structured, Resume/Start-shell, replay, binding-less crash retry), plus the rendered QA tool with screenshots.
After that, the upstream DRAFT PR to stablyai/orca follows the repo template, with Visual Proof from the QA screenshots.
